From 4019797503535f2587e870be40e4d285c9974003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:04:52 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] feat(agent): the agent asks before what cannot be
 undone, and a like lives with its song

A like moves from one window's local storage into the song's own metadata, so the
library carries it to every window and to the agent (metadata.liked, GET
/v1/library/liked, POST /v1/library/songs/{id}/liked); the old list is moved once,
the first time the window opens after the change.

The studio keeps permissions and a leash - free, risky (the default) or all - set
in Settings, Agent (MCP). A question reaches the window as a modal with five
answers: once, this session, always, ask every time, never. An answer is kept per
action and scope (session:<id> or always), so the same thing is asked once, and
both the question and the answer land in the message log.

The MCP tools agent_permissions and agent_leash show what was decided, and every
changing tool passes the leash first - the agent never widens its own leash, only
the person in front of the window answers. The MCP skill and IDEA.md say the same,
and every new string is on the five languages the studio speaks.
